<!-- LLM-driven agent in CARLA -->
<p>
  I built an LLM-driven driving agent in CARLA. The agent receives both state information 
  (e.g., speed, forward vector, and navigation command) and visual input (RGB and bird’s-eye-view images). 
  These inputs are passed into a large language model (LLM) with a structured prompt that requests 
  driving actions in JSON format. The model outputs continuous control signals—throttle, steering, and brake—
  which are applied to the vehicle in real time. As shown below, the agent demonstrates smooth and 
  stable driving behavior while responding to language-based navigation commands.
</p>

